That covers, for each theme: the colour palette (colors.toml) and the application theme files made from it (btop.theme,
hyprland.lua, chromium.theme, icons.theme, keyboard.rgb, shell.lock.toml), the preview and lock-screen images, the wallpapers
(which are drawn by the generator scripts in themes/generators/ and so exist as files only after install-themes or
make-wallpapers has run), and the THEME.md texts.

You may share and adapt all of it, including commercially, as long as you give appropriate credit, link to the licence and say
if you changed anything. A suitable credit line:

    Omarchy Kit themes by Aldo Ruiz Luna, https://github.com/aldoruizluna/omarchy-kit, CC BY 4.0

The generator scripts themselves (themes/generators/, themes/make-wallpapers, themes/install-themes) are code and fall under the
MIT licence of the repository (see the LICENSE file at the top).

The open-source works credited in each THEME.md inspired the look of these themes; none of their files, art or palettes were copied,
and this licence says nothing about them. No official artwork, logo or character likeness of any brand is included.
